      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To establish RP-HPLC method for determination of atropine sulphate, diphenhydramine hydrochloride, capsaicin and dihydrocapsaicin in pain-relieving plaster for arthritis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "The sample were separated on an Alltima C18 Column (4.6 mm x 250 mm, 5 microm) with the moblie phase of CH3 CN-0.1% H3 PO4. Flow rate was 1 mL x min(-1). The detective wavelength was set at 210 and 280 nm. Column temperature was 30 degrees C."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULT",
          "content": "The calibration curve for atropine sulphate, diphenhydramine hydrochloride, capsaicin and dihydrocapsaicin revealed linearity in the range of 2.01-50.25, 15.08-377.00, 5.02-125.50, 5.03-125.75 mg x L(-1), respectively. The recoveries of atropine sulphate, diphenhydramine hydrochloride, capsaicin and dihydrocapsaicin were 99.00% with RSD of 0.95%, 99.89% with RSD of 1.2%, 100.1% with RSD of 1.5% and 99.51%, with RSD of 1.4%, respectively."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The method is simple, rapid and accurate, which is suitable for the quality control of pain-relieving plaster for arthritis."
        }
      ]},
